evals.prompt:
Write src/managers/TickerManager.ts for our exchange websocket (wss://feed.example.com). On connect it sends `{ type: 'snapshot', tickers: [...] }` with ~300 tickers, then `{ type: 'ticker', product_id, price, volume }` one at a time. Get both into the Data Client store so `useQuery(Ticker, { product_id })` updates. Ticker is in src/resources/Ticker.ts:

```ts
import { Entity } from '@data-client/rest';
export class Ticker extends Entity {
  product_id = '';
  price = 0;
  volume = 0;
  pk() { return this.product_id; }
  static key = 'Ticker';
}
```

our ticker feed pushes ~500 msgs/sec and calling controller.set on every message is tanking perf. can you change the manager so it buffers messages and flushes to the store every 100ms? each message is `{ product_id, price, volume }` and the entity is `Ticker` (pk is product_id) from src/resources/Ticker.ts. current code:

```ts
import type { Manager, Middleware } from '@data-client/react';
import { Ticker } from '../resources/Ticker';

export default class TickerManager implements Manager {
  declare protected ws: WebSocket;
  middleware: Middleware = controller => {
    this.ws = new WebSocket('wss://feed.example.com');
    this.ws.onmessage = e => {
      const msg = JSON.parse(e.data);
      controller.set(Ticker, { product_id: msg.product_id }, msg);
    };
    return next => async action => next(action);
  };
  cleanup() { this.ws.close(); }
}
```
